 ("h2", "1. Why Do We Need Political Parties?"),
 ("p", "For most ordinary citizens, democracy is equal to political parties. A villager may know nothing about the Constitution but will know something about parties. This visibility does not mean popularity: people blame parties for all that is wrong with democracy. About a hundred years ago few countries had parties; today almost every country has them."),
