 ("p", "Even in non-party panchayat elections in many States, villages split into factions and each puts up a panel of candidates, which is exactly what a party does. The rise of parties is linked to the emergence of representative democracy: large and complex societies need an agency to gather views, bring representatives together, form a responsible government, and support or restrain it. Parties fulfil these needs, so they are a **necessary condition for democracy**."),
